WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.900
1 · Start a request.

2
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.400
In New chat, describe the data you need in plain English.

3
00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.000
Press Send, and the run starts right away.

4
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:15.300
Already have the data? Upload a CSV or Excel file instead.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.300
2 · AWDAX plans the run. This is the sample run, with fictional data.

6
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.500
It searches the web and checks each source.

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:23.100
Then it inspects the pages and plans how to read them.

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.900
3 · Watch the live run: rows arrive page by page.

9
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.100
Everything is merged into one table, with a report.

10
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:32.800
Web requests keep refreshing every 5 minutes.

11
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:36.400
4 · Read your project reports.

12
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:41.300
Projects report lists every request and upload, with its status, rows and last update.

13
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.700
Open a chat. Report shows totals and charts built from your rows.

14
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.400
Data lists every row, with the page it came from.

15
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.000
Graphs turns the rows into charts you can add and edit.

16
00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:58.900
Sources shows each website, how it was read, and what it gave.

17
00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.400
Ask a question in words, right under the dashboard.

18
00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.400
The answer comes from these rows, exactly. Nothing is scraped again.

19
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.500
Export the data when you need it somewhere else.

20
00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.700
CSV, Excel, JSON, SQL and more.

21
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.100
That’s it. Start a new chat whenever you’re ready.
